<title>GERMANY: Pan-German March numbers in work rise.</title>
<headline>Pan-German March numbers in work rise.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>PAN-GERMAN NUMBERS IN WORK		 Mar 97   Feb 97   Mar 96</p>
<p> Number in work (1)(unadj, million)    33.830   33.702   34.273</p>
<p> Number in work (1)(seas adj, million) 34.022   33.979   34.467</p>
<p> Number in work (2)(seas adj, million) 34.058   34.016   34.509</p>
<p>WEST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj,million)	  27.783   27.671   28.104</p>
<p> Number in work (seas adj, million)    27.935   27.910   28.256</p>
<p>EAST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj, million)	  6.058    6.035    6.187</p>
<p> Number in work (seas adj, million)     6.123    6.106    6.253</p>
<p>NOTE - Pan-German figure marked (1) refer to people living in Germany. Those marked (2), as well as all the west and east German figures, refer to people working in the respective regions but not necessarily living in Germany.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
